:XuiGetNextCallback()
###################################
#####  XuiGetNextCallback ()  #####
###################################

	XuiGetNextCallback (@grid, @message$, @v0, @v1, @v2, @v3, @winkid, @gridName$)
	win = winkid >> 16
	kid = winkid AND 0xFFFF

	This function is used in the "convenience function message loop"
	in most standard GUI programs to remove messages from the callback
	message queue. Messages are put in the queue by XuiQueueCallbacks()
	when it is specified in the SetCallback message such as follows:

	XuiSendMessage (grid, #SetCallback, callGrid, &XuiQueueCallbacks(), v2, v3, win, r1)

	Values supplied in v2 and v3 are returned in XuiGetNextCallback()
	unless they are set to -1 in which case the values from the callback
	are passed through.
	The win, if set in r0, is shifted left 16 bits and OR'd with the kid from
	the Callback to be the winkid in the XuiGetNextCallback(). Demo program
	"aeasy.x" demonstrates how this is used.

	See: SetCallback, XuiCallback(), XuiGetCallback(), XuiQueueCallbacks(), XuiSetCallback()

FUNCTION  XuiGetNextCallback (grid, message$, v0, v1, v2, v3, r0, r1$)
