:XuiSetGridFunction()
###################################
#####  XuiSetGridFunction ()  #####
###################################

	error = XuiSetGridFunction (grid, #SetGridFunction, &gridFunc(), 0, 0, 0, kid, 0)

	Replaces the grid function address that was set by XuiCreateGrid()
	when a window and its grids were created.

	CAUTION: Remember to put the "&" at the beginning and the "()"
	at the end of the function name, so that it is the address of a
	function and no the content or address of a variable.

	XuiSetGridFunction() calls XgrSetGridFunction() so that the
	Graphics program has identical grid function address.

	See: SetGridFunction, XgrSetGridFunction()

FUNCTION  XuiSetGridFunction (grid, message, v0, v1, v2, v3, kid, r1)
